}, {"id": 1873033, "url": "//images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_thumb/sc1458p.jpg"}], "slug": "perfect-thog", "summary": "Perfect THoG is a game about placing gems unto a grid. When the arrange phase completes, THoGs are scored, and a round-winner declared.\n\nPlace in the arrange phase...\n\nScore in the THoG phase...\n\nCompete for perfection in Versus puzzle action, or in Perfect single player modes (such as Forever).\n\nBecome perfect.\n\n6 THoGs: Frog Water, Fire, Cardinal Earth, Jordo the Last, Inscrutable Wizard Glibbyr, and Roadside Duality.\n\nUnto this perfect grid, the 6 by 6 by 6 space will be filled by alternating gems!\n\nNew interpolation of perfect-imperfection; a big-bang but tiny and not-real!\n\nThe fifth game by Sam Atlas, music by DL Salo", "themes": [{"id": 18, "name": "Science fiction"}], "url": "https://www.igdb.com/games/perfect-thog"}